Name: Adi Charan  
IDE: Google Colab / VS Code  

Dataset Source: Kaggle (IPL Ball-by-Ball Data)

Datasets Used:

1. deliveries_updated_mens_ipl_upto_2024.csv  
   • Number of Rows: 260,920  
   • Number of Columns: 20  
   • Description: Ball-by-ball IPL data (batsman runs, extras, wickets, teams, bowler info)

2. ball.csv  
   • Number of Rows: 278,205  
   • Number of Columns: 30  
   • Description: Raw IPL ball-by-ball dataset used for validation and feature extraction

3. batsman_match_features (Generated)  
   • Number of Rows: Varies by player  
   • Number of Columns: 10  
   • Description: Batsman-level aggregated features (avg5, avg10, career avg, strike rate)

4. bowler_match_features (Generated)  
   • Number of Rows: Varies by player  
   • Number of Columns: 8  
   • Description: Bowler-level aggregated features (avg5, avg10, career avg, economy etc.)

5. match_dates (Generated)  
   • Number of Rows: Unique Match IDs  
   • Number of Columns: 2  
   • Description: Match and date mapping used for time-series features

6. Model Files  
   • batsman_runs_model.pkl  
   • bowler_wickets_model.pkl  
   • Description: Trained Random Forest models for predicting runs & wickets
